Z||000000||stimpy||11-12-2000||07:38 PM||||Well, FCO meetingwas this afternoon and got some interesting news.  A new member who relocated from Chicago was there in his 86 2M4 with a Porsche 944 front end kit! I'm telling you, it was cool! He doesn't have anything yet to box out the back to match, but he's still working on it.<BR>Also talked to the guy from Minco who is getting ito the 3.8 business. He is getting started right now doing a swap into one of the members 88 coupe, using the 5 speed.  I'm dying to see how it turns out.  Well, that's the scoop. Talk to y'all later.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||GarethWright||11-14-2000||02:08 AM||||Hey Stimpy, I am in Broken Arrow (about 500 ft from Tulsa, OK.)  The FCO meetings are in Norman right?  Who would I call/write to about joining FCO?, and could you let me know the date/time of the next meeting? Thanks in advance, Gareth<P>Lol And I know for a fact my Fiero Will make it to Norman, as I drove to OU to visit a bud a few weeks ago  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||11-14-2000||10:23 AM||||Well, I can tell you what you need to know.  Meetings are held 2nd Sunday of every month at Favorite's Restaurant at 6318 S. Shields Ave in OKC (not Norman. We have our annual show in Norman, but meetings in OKC). As of Sunday's meeting, they are instituting a tuesday night meeting, last Tuesday of each month. I think the Sunday afternoon might be more practical for you, but everyone is welcome at any of our meetings.<BR>Look forward to seeing you next month!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||GarethWright||11-14-2000||09:22 PM||||ok thanks for the info, I may be able to make the Dec 10th meeting depending on the weather.  Hope to see ya there If I make it.||||reg||1
